\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The sign of a one-dimensional paired insertion}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the rank-one [paired algebra](fdip-00TJ),
write its generators as #{\psi,\bar\psi}. Its top generator
is #{\Omega=\psi\bar\psi}, so
#{\mathcal I(\psi\bar\psi)=1}.
For #{K=\kappa\bbI} and a scalar #{c},
##{\extexp(\theta_K)=1+\kappa\psi\bar\psi,\qquad
 \mathcal I\bigl(c\bar\psi\psi\,
       \extexp(\theta_K)\bigr)=-c.}
Every word of degree greater than two vanishes, and
#{\bar\psi\psi=-\psi\bar\psi}. If #{\kappa} is a unit,
the normalized coefficient is #{-c/\kappa}.
Here #{c} can be the scalar transport in a
[dressed pair](fdip-00WD). Reversing the order of its two
odd fields reverses this sign.}
